alyst_adjustment": -1.8, "key_factors": ["Strong Republican district (R+9 partisan lean) with long-serving incumbent Virginia Foxx", "Overwhelming expert consensus, ranging from Likely R to Safe R across ten raters", "Large financial advantage for Foxx ($3.5M cash) over challenger Chuck Hubbard", "No public general-election polling; prediction markets price Democratic chances near 12%"], "rationale": "The fundamentals point firmly to Foxx: a +9 Republican district, incumbency, and a dominant fundraising edge, with every major rater placing the race at Likely R or better and markets giving Hubbard roughly a one-in-eight chance. The forecast shifts modestly toward the Safe R consensus while retaining uncertainty from the absence of polling.", "watch": "Any late surge in Democratic spending or polling showing Hubbard within single digits would warrant moving the race toward Tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Virginia Foxx (R) is running."]}, "overview": "North Carolina's 5th District is a Republican-leaning seat in the state's northwestern corner, and Virginia Foxx has held it for many years. She enters the general election with a large war chest of about $3.5 million, while Democratic nominee Chuck Hubbard has raised a modest sum and trails badly in cash on hand. A Libertarian is also on the ballot.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the picture rests on the district's Republican lean, Foxx's incumbency, and outside assessments. Rating outlets uniformly place the race at Likely R or Safe R, and prediction markets give Hubbard only about a one-in-eight chance. Foxx has campaigned on constituent services and disaster recovery legislation, with little sign of a competitive race developing.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0624, "margin": -9.74}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0488, "margin": -11.5}, {"date": "2026-09-2